WEBVTT

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:04.980
Harvest-now, decrypt-later is a defensive threat model for long-term confidentiality.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.700
The idea is that an adversary may collect encrypted data today, store it,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.960
and wait for a future point when decryption becomes easier or feasible.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.185
The attacker may not be able to read the data now.

00:00:14.185 --> 00:00:16.760
The risk exists because the data may still be sensitive later,

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.860
while cryptanalytic techniques, computing capability, implementation knowledge,

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.860
or available tooling may improve over time.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.265
This is different from immediate compromise.

00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:28.840
In an immediate compromise, the protected information is exposed now because an account,

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.020
system, key, application, or protocol fails in the present.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.820
In harvest-now, decrypt-later planning,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.780
the concern is future exposure of data that seemed protected at the time it was collected.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.020
That distinction matters because it changes how teams think about retention,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.310
data lifetime, cryptographic choices, and migration timing.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.430
Future quantum computing is one reason this model receives attention,

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:51.590
especially for data protected by public-key cryptography that may be considered vulnerable

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.620
to cryptographically relevant quantum capabilities.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.300
Quantum computing is not the only possible source of future risk,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.240
and responsible planning should avoid countdowns or panic.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.840
The practical question is simpler: if encrypted information is copied today,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.125
how long must it remain confidential, and what assumptions protect it?

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:10.800
This course treats harvest-now, decrypt-later as a defensive planning topic.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.340
The goal is not to intercept traffic, steal data, or attempt unauthorized decryption.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.060
The goal is to help security, engineering, legal, privacy, operations,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.450
and leadership teams identify long-lived sensitive information,

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.710
understand how cryptography protects it,

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:29.120
and reduce future confidentiality risk before emergency migration becomes necessary.
